{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "נגח", :translit "nagach", :gloss "gored"} {:he "ב' במס' הכא", :translit "bet be-masorah kan", :gloss "two in the Masorah here"} {:he "או נודע כי שור נגח הוא", :translit "o noda ki shor nagach hu", :gloss "or it is known that an ox is a gorer"} {:he "שור שנגח", :translit "shor she-nagach", :gloss "an ox that gored"} {:he "נזקין ממיתה", :translit "nezikin mi-mitah", :gloss "damages from death [cases]"} {:he "על הקטנים כגדולים", :translit "al ha-ketanim ka-gedolim", :gloss "for minors as for adults"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["נגח" "או נודע כי שור נגח הוא"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah: learning damages from capital cases"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'shor she-nagach' refers to the talmudic chapter in tractate Bava Kamma dealing with goring oxen. There, the Sages derive civil damages (nezikin) from capital cases (mitah) by a hermeneutical link: just as in capital law there is no distinction between killing an adult or a minor, so too in damages one is obligated equally for killing a minor as an adult (Bava Kamma 83b-84a). Ba'al HaTurim notes that the doubled word 'nagach' supports drawing this legal parallel.", :sources ["Bava Kamma 83b" "Bava Kamma 84a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["נגח" "או נודע כי שור נגח הוא"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "נגח", :refs ["Exodus 21:29" "Exodus 21:36"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "או נודע כי שור נגח הוא", :refs ["Exodus 21:36"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah: learning damages from capital cases", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:14.545900997Z", :model "glm-5.2"}